---
/**
 * /youtube-api/audit (keyword map C98, W1). Google facts: revision history and getting started, checked 2026-11-12.
 * Siar facts: docs/approvals/google.md. Siar has not confirmed a public upload (strike-plan.md §2 row 7).
 */
import Article from '../../layouts/Article.astro';
import SiarBox from '../../components/network/SiarBox.astro';
import StatusLine from '../../components/network/StatusLine.astro';
import NetFacts from '../../components/network/NetFacts.astro';
import { CHECKED, LIVE } from '../../components/network/data';

const REV = 'https://developers.google.com/youtube/v3/revision_history';
const GS = 'https://developers.google.com/youtube/v3/getting-started';
const hpw = (a: string) => (LIVE.howPublishing ? `/how-publishing-works#${a}` : '/docs/errors');
const faq = [
  { q: 'Are YouTube API uploads still locked private before the audit?', a: "No, not since 2 November 2026. Google's revision history says videos uploaded through <code>videos.insert</code> from unverified API projects are no longer restricted to private viewing mode, and an upload with no privacy set defaults to public. Some uploads can still default to private because of the channel's own settings." },
  { q: 'Do I still need the YouTube API audit?', a: "For more quota, yes. The default allocation is small for an app that uploads for many channels, and more quota is requested with Google's quota extension form, which reviews how the project uses the API. The 2 November change removed the private-only rule, not the quota limit." },
  { q: 'How long does the YouTube API audit take?', a: "Google does not publish a time. Siar's request was submitted on 15 October 2026 and acknowledged on 16 October 2026; on 12 November 2026 it was still in review, with no questions from Google so far." },
  { q: 'Can videos uploaded before 2 November 2026 be made public now?', a: "Google's 2 November entry covers new uploads; it does not say whether earlier uploads can be switched to public. Try it on one video in YouTube Studio before relying on it." },
];
---
<Article
  metaTitle="YouTube API audit: what changed on 2 November 2026"
  h1="YouTube API audit and quota extension: what changed on 2 November 2026"
  description="Uploads from unaudited YouTube API projects are no longer forced to private since 2 November 2026. What the audit still decides, and where Siar's stands."
  kicker="YouTube API"
  updated={CHECKED}
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Platforms', href: '/platforms' }, { name: 'YouTube API', href: '/youtube-api' }, { name: 'Audit', href: '/youtube-api/audit' }]}
  lead={'Since 2 November 2026, YouTube no longer forces uploads from unaudited API projects to private; an upload with no privacy set now defaults to public. The audit still decides how much quota a project gets. Siar, a <a href="/">unified social media API</a>, has its audit in review and has not yet confirmed a public upload.'}
  faq={faq}
  actions="quickstart"
>
  <StatusLine type="YOUTUBE" slug="youtube" />

  <h2 id="change">The 2 November 2026 change</h2>
  <p>Until 2 November 2026, every video uploaded through <code>videos.insert</code> by a project that had not passed YouTube's API compliance audit was locked to private. Google lifted that rule. On 3 November 2026 Google also added custom thumbnails for Shorts.</p>
  <NetFacts facts={[
    { text: 'Videos uploaded through the <code>videos.insert</code> method from unverified API projects "are no longer restricted to private viewing mode"; when <code>status.privacyStatus</code> is not set the video defaults to public, and "certain uploads might default to private based on creator account settings".', url: REV, source: 'Google, YouTube Data API revision history (2 November 2026)' },
  ]} />
  <p>If an upload still comes back private, check the channel's default upload visibility in YouTube Studio and set <code>status.privacyStatus</code> on every request.</p>

  <h2 id="what-audit-decides">What the audit still decides</h2>
  <p>The audit is now about quota and policy, not visibility. More quota is requested with Google's quota extension form, and Google reviews how the project uses YouTube data against its developer policies before granting it.</p>
  <NetFacts facts={[{ text: 'Projects get a default allocation of 10,000 units a day plus separate <code>videos.insert</code> and <code>search.list</code> allocations; more is requested with the quota extension form.', url: GS, source: 'Google, YouTube Data API getting started' }]} />
  <p><a href="/youtube-api/quota">YouTube Data API quota, explained</a> covers the numbers and the <code>quotaExceeded</code> error.</p>

  <h2 id="what-we-filed">What Siar filed, and what it built for it</h2>
  <p>Siar's request went in on 15 October 2026, the day Google approved its OAuth verification for <code>youtube.upload</code> and <code>youtube.force-ssl</code>. The form asked about the organization, the audience, each API client and every endpoint used. Siar listed 22 endpoints, never <code>search.list</code>.</p>
  <p>The compliance work before submitting, checked against YouTube's developer policies:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>A "Data from YouTube" section in the privacy policy: YouTube's terms and Google's privacy policy linked, what is read and stored, retention, and the link to revoke access.</li>
    <li>YouTube's terms and Google's privacy policy on the connect screen, in the dashboard and on the hosted connect page.</li>
    <li>Data retention: imported YouTube comments and history deleted after 30 days unless refreshed, and everything read from a removed channel wiped.</li>
    <li>A demo film of the consent screen and each scope in use.</li>
  </ul>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Date</th><th>Siar and Google</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>2026-10-15</td><td>OAuth verification approved; API audit and quota request submitted</td></tr>
      <tr><td>2026-10-16</td><td>Google acknowledged the request</td></tr>
      <tr><td>2026-11-02</td><td>Google lifted the private-only rule for unaudited projects</td></tr>
      <tr><td>2026-11-12</td><td>Audit still in review; no public upload confirmed through Siar yet</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>

  <SiarBox items={[
    'Siar sends the visibility you ask for. If YouTube returns private anyway, Siar adds a warning to the post instead of reporting it as public.',
    'Uploads run through Siar\'s verified Google project, so your customers file nothing with Google.',
    `If YouTube says no, you get its own reason and message, plus the fix: <a href="${hpw('errors')}">the network's own error</a>.`,
  ]} />
  <p class="small">Related: <a href="/youtube-api">YouTube upload API guide</a> · <a href="/youtube-api/errors#code-privacystatus-private">YouTube private upload error</a> · <a href="/platforms">Network status</a>{LIVE.approvals && <> · <a href="/platforms/approvals#youtube">YouTube approval record</a></>}</p>
</Article>
